<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill starts two life insurers.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill starts two life insurers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch said analyst Edward Spehar  initiated coverage of Nationwide Financial Services Inc and Hartford  Life Inc.</p>
<p>-- Spehar was not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Merrill said Nationwide Financial was started with a near-term  accumulate and long-term buy rating. Hartford Life was started with  a near-term and long-term accumulate rating.</p>
<p>-- Nationwide Financial rose 1/8 to 30-3/8 and Hartford Life rose  1/8 to 41-1/4.</p>
</text>
